              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "قطار — qatār — \"a queue; a row\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ٹکٹ کے لیے لمبی قطار تھی۔ ṭikaṭ ke liye lambī qatār thī. There was a long queue for tickets."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "is usually traced, through Persian, to Arabic qiṭār, \"a line of camels\"; in Urdu any line of people waiting is a قطار (qatār)."
            }
          ]
        },
